## Python Instruction
Write a python function to check if two strings are almost equal. Two strings are considered almost equal if you can swap two letters in one of them so that the result is equal to the second string.

## Python Solution
```python
def are_almost_equal(s1: str, s2: str) -> bool:
    if s1 == s2:
        return True
    diff = []
    for i in range(len(s1)):
        if s1[i] != s2[i]:
            diff.append([s1[i], s2[i]])
    if len(diff) != 2:
        return False
    return diff[0] == diff[1][::-1]
```

## Python Tests
assert are_almost_equal("attack", "defend") == False
assert are_almost_equal("bank", "kanb") == True
assert are_almost_equal("kelb", "kelb") == True

